      "raw_payload": {
        "id": "R1",
        "kind": "hypothesis",
        "claim": "Speculative capability: the weakly magnetic spare could retain its position and support a gloved swap through a mechanically indexed pocket whose opening gate also provides an edge-free handling point.",
        "delta": "Change the retention dependency from magnetic attraction or friction to contact boundaries. Bolt drilled steel strips through the existing slots; form side capture and end stops behind the marked edge, with a movable fourth-strip gate. Wire may keep the gate hardware recoverable. Plate pickup must use an accessible unmarked surface; the gate is not assumed to lift it.",
        "prediction": "Nearest rival: a cork-lined strip clamp using friction alone. If geometric capture supplies retention, the spare should remain within 1 mm even with only light seating pressure, while the friction clamp may drift when its pressure is reduced. Equal success would leave that distinction unresolved; cage drift, trapped extraction, or slow gloved servicing defeats the proposed capability.",
        "probe": "First map slots, clearance, exposed edge and unmarked pickup access using ruler and marker. Verify strip bendability, bolt fit and sub-millimetre pocket play before fabrication; abandon if unavailable geometry prevents capture. Within eighty minutes, build at most the pocket and cork-clamp rival using supplied strips, bolts and pads. Within twenty observation minutes, use ruler and stroke counter for up to three twenty-stroke runs per configuration, recording displacement and seating pressure qualitatively. Include the spare in the final twenty-stroke run. Time up to three removal/return checks per configuration with thick gloves, requiring no marked-edge contact and completion within sixty seconds. A pull-scale comparison up to 10 N can characterize escape paths, but cannot establish resistance to unknown stroke forces. Stop early on clearance intrusion or edge-contact necessity.",
        "fit": "uncertain",
        "assumptions": [
          "Slot dimensions and locations permit mounting outside stroke clearance.",
          "Strips can be formed with supplied pliers and provide sufficient stiffness.",
          "Available bolts and strips support capture and a gloved gate without modifying plate or carriage.",
          "Stroke duration allows informative comparisons within twenty minutes; otherwise fewer runs reduce confidence."
        ],
        "source_refs": [
